# What reaches the public main. An allowlist, not a denylist, so a new internal file stays
# private by default. One path or glob per line. Read by scripts/release.mjs.
#
# Never add: TASKS.md, OPERATOR_TODO.md, FEASIBILITY.md, CLAUDE.md, .claude/, spikes/,
# docs/plans/, scratch files. The release job fails on those markers anyway.

# Code and its unit tests. Tests stay public: "quality of the code" is judged, and tests are
# the evidence.
apps/**
packages/**

# The benchmark. The claims are only credible if a sceptic can rerun them from the public repo.
benchmark/**

# What the public tests read. Without these the published suite installs, builds, and then fails 6
# of 17 on ENOENT, which is worse than shipping no tests: it tells a judge who cloned the repo that
# the code is broken. The recorder redacts credentials on the way in, checked: the only api-key in
# here is the literal `api-key=REDACTED`, and neither live key appears in any of the 44 files.
#
# fixtures/golden is deliberately NOT here. It is hand-verified ledgers from the team's own test
# wallets, so publishing it publishes real addresses and their full trading history. It holds only
# a README today, so this costs nothing yet; whoever lands the first golden ledger decides, and
# leaving it out means the decision has to be made on purpose rather than by a glob.
fixtures/contracts/**
fixtures/recorded/**

# Public docs and the quickstart.
README.md
LICENSE
.env.example
docs/public/**

# Workspace files the stripped tree needs to install and build on its own. Measured, not guessed:
# without tsconfig.json `pnpm build` is TS5083 on the missing solution file, and without
# vitest.config.ts `pnpm test` exits 1 with "No test files found" because the three projects that
# carry passWithNoTests are gone. Both legs of the release job failed on the stripped tree until
# these two lines existed.
package.json
pnpm-workspace.yaml
pnpm-lock.yaml
tsconfig.json
tsconfig.base.json
vitest.config.ts
knip.json

# One public CI workflow, so judges see the tests run on the repo they cloned.
.github/workflows/public-ci.yml
